@page "/privacy"
@using Shoppet_VetClinic.Components.Layout
@layout LandingLayout

<PageTitle>Data Privacy Notice | ShoppetCare</PageTitle>

<div class="legal-page">
    <main class="legal-shell">
        <span class="legal-kicker">DATA PRIVACY</span>
        <h1>ShoppetCare Data Privacy Notice</h1>
        <p class="legal-lead">
            This notice explains what information the current ShoppetCare pilot uses and why. The project should collect
            only information needed for its pet-care, marketplace, community, and Premium workflows.
        </p>

        <section>
            <h2>Information used by the platform</h2>
            <p>
                Account information may include name, email address, mobile number, role, account status, and Premium
                references. Pet-care information may include pet identity, birth date, weight, diet, vaccination and health
                records, Digital Pet ID information, and uploaded pet images. Marketplace, Community,
                notification, and transaction records are also stored when those features are used.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Why the information is used</h2>
            <p>
                Information is used to authenticate accounts, connect pet records across ShoppetCare features, generate
                Digital Pet IDs, manage marketplace and community content, record
                simulated Premium and marketplace payments, and show relevant notifications.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Public and private information</h2>
            <p>
                Public marketplace listings, and community posts are visible according to their feature
                design. Public Pet ID pages show limited identity information and an owner phone number only when the owner opts in.
                Private diet and health information are hidden. Private pet-care records remain account-controlled.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Mock payment information</h2>
            <p>
                The academic checkout stores the selected mock payment method, amount, project reference number, status,
                and date. It does not connect to GCash, Maya, banks, card networks, or a production payment gateway.
                Real card credentials should never be entered or stored.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Uploads</h2>
            <p>
                User-uploaded images are limited to supported image formats and are used only for the feature in which
                they were uploaded, such as pet profiles, marketplace listings, or community posts.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Access and correction</h2>
            <p>
                Users can update supported account and profile information through the platform. For project data that
                cannot be edited directly in the interface, the project administrator can review the record during the
                academic pilot.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Project security and limitations</h2>
            <p>
                ShoppetCare uses account-based access controls and ownership checks for protected workflows. As an academic
                pilot, it should not be treated as a production medical-record, financial, or emergency-response system.
            </p>
        </section>

        <div class="legal-actions">
            <a href="/terms">Read Terms &amp; Conditions</a>
            <a href="/register" class="primary">Create Account</a>
        </div>
    </main>
</div>

<style>
    .legal-page{min-height:100vh;padding:54px 24px;background:#FAF9F6;color:#1E2D27}
    .legal-shell{width:min(920px,100%);margin:auto;padding:44px;border:1px solid #E1E8E5;border-radius:24px;background:#fff;box-shadow:0 18px 50px rgba(30,45,39,.06)}
    .legal-kicker{color:#2F9098;font-size:.7rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.12em}
    .legal-shell h1{margin:8px 0 10px;font-size:clamp(2.4rem,5vw,4rem);font-weight:900;letter-spacing:-.05em}
    .legal-lead{font-size:1rem;color:#65746E;line-height:1.7}
    .legal-shell section{padding:22px 0;border-top:1px solid #EDF1EF}
    .legal-shell h2{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:850}
    .legal-shell p{margin:0;color:#5E6D67;line-height:1.72}
    .legal-actions{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:24px}
    .legal-actions a{padding:12px 18px;border:1px solid #C9D9D5;border-radius:10px;color:#173D3D;text-decoration:none;font-weight:800}
    .legal-actions .primary{background:#2F9098;border-color:#2F9098;color:#fff}
    @@media(max-width:640px){.legal-shell{padding:26px}}
</style>
